; Belt rounds on the hud model. bullet1_<k+1> stays visible while at least k rounds are
; left, so the belt empties from bullet1_12 down to bullet1_2 and the last round leaves
; bullet1_2 alone; at 0 every link is bare. The links themselves (bullet1..bullet11) are
; never touched. The count here is what the MAGAZINE shows -- the chambered round is
; excluded by the engine, so 101 loaded reads as 100 here.
misfire_start_condition = 0
condition_shot_dec      = 0.0001
misfire_probability     = 0.001
misfire_condition_k     = 0.01
[wpn_pkm_ammo_bones]
; What appears and disappears is the CARTRIDGE in each belt link, not the link itself:
; the hud model nests bullet1_2 under bullet1, bullet1_3 under bullet2 ... bullet1_12 under
; bullet11 (all links parented to `mag`). Driving the links hid the rounds too, because
; set_bone_visible recurses into children -- so the whole belt vanished instead of emptying.
; 11 links are driven now, against 9 before.
